This issue occurs because when you submit a batch successfully, the modal closes, but the states controlling the "Action Screen" (isActionMode, actionSelection, etc.) are not being reset back to their default values. When you open the next batch, it remembers that isActionMode was true and actionSelection was "ACCEPTED".
To fix this completely, we need to reset these states whenever you **open** a new modal, and also when a submission is **successful**.
Here are the two exact code replacements to fix this state leak:
### 1. Reset State when Opening the View Modal
**Find this exact code block (around line 431):**
```javascript
  const handleOpenViewModal = async (row) => {
    setViewingBatch(row);
    setViewingBatchId(row.batchId);
    setViewingBatchCreatorId(String(row.creatorId));
    setViewingBatchState(row.workflowState || "");
    setViewingBatchOrder(row.currentOrder || 1);

    setIsViewModalOpen(true);
    setIsFetchingSteps(true);
    setIsFetchingVid(true);

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
  const handleOpenViewModal = async (row) => {
    // --- FIX: Reset all action screen states to guarantee a clean slate ---
    setIsActionMode(false);
    setActionSelection(null);
    setExecutorRemarks("");
    setScheduleOverrideType("KEEP");
    setFinalScheduleTime("");
    setIsDescExpanded(false);

    setViewingBatch(row);
    setViewingBatchId(row.batchId);
    setViewingBatchCreatorId(String(row.creatorId));
    setViewingBatchState(row.workflowState || "");
    setViewingBatchOrder(row.currentOrder || 1);

    setIsViewModalOpen(true);
    setIsFetchingSteps(true);
    setIsFetchingVid(true);

```
### 2. Reset State upon Successful Submission
**Find this exact block inside your handleSubmitAction function (around line 603):**
```javascript
      showSnackBar(
        response?.message || "Workflow action processed successfully.",
        "success"
      );

      setIsScheduleLapseModalOpen(false);
      setIsViewModalOpen(false);
      setNewScheduleTime("");
      setExecutorRemarks("");
      fetchPendingBatches();

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
      showSnackBar(
        response?.message || "Workflow action processed successfully.",
        "success"
      );

      setIsScheduleLapseModalOpen(false);
      setIsViewModalOpen(false);
      
      // --- FIX: Reset action states so the modal is completely reset for the next time ---
      setIsActionMode(false);
      setActionSelection(null);
      setScheduleOverrideType("KEEP");
      setFinalScheduleTime("");
      
      setNewScheduleTime("");
      setExecutorRemarks("");
      fetchPendingBatches();

```
By adding these resets, the UI will be forced to forget the previous batch's selections, and every time you click "View & Action" on a new batch, it will correctly start on the Details screen!
